to</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<pre>size(200); \nimport olympiad; \n\n//definitions \npair A=origin, B=(4,0), C=(4,2), D=(0,2), E=(2,2); \npath p1=(A--C); \npath p2=(E--B); \n\n//draw \ndraw(A--B--C--D--cycle); \ndraw(p1); \ndraw(p2); \ndot((A)); \ndot((B)); \ndot((C)); \ndot((D)); \ndot((E)); \ndot((IP(p1,p2))); \n\n//label \nlabel(\"A\",A,SW); \nlabel(\"B\",B,SE); \nlabel(\"C\",C,NE); \nlabel(\"D\",D,NW); \nlabel(\"E\",E,N); \nlabel(\"F\", IP(p1,p2),S);\n</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e12e1e5e99aafb5989d76c97840afa2474e1cdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200);  import olympiad;   //definitions  pair A=origin, B=(4,0), C=(4,2), D=(0,2), E=(2,2);  path p1=(A--C);  path p2=(E--B);   //draw  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);  draw(p1);  draw(p2);  dot((A));  dot((B));  dot((C));  dot((D));  dot((E));  dot((IP(p1,p2)));   //label  label(&quot;A&quot;,A,SW);  label(&quot;B&quot;,B,SE);  label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NE);  label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NW);  label(&quot;E&quot;,E,N);  label(&quot;F&quot;, IP(p1,p2),S); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p>For definitions, see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Olympiad_Package_Part_1\" title=\"Asymptote: Olympiad Package Part 1\">Olympiad Package Part 1: Value Setting</a>.\n</p><p>For drawing, see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Drawing\" title=\"Asymptote: Drawing\">Drawing</a>.\n</p><p>For labeling, see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Labeling\" title=\"Asymptote: Labeling\">Labeling</a>.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018073827\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 793/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1006/5000000 bytes\